  "scientific_review": [
    "All six Atlantic/Pacific/Indian SEC cases retain every one of thirty original section anchors, including unselected, gate/support-edge and vertically censored cases. Raw-profile/diagnosis pointers, source coordinates and primary depths/spans remain unchanged from pinned cloud source artifacts. Unsupported cases stay explicit.",
    "Each basin has its own owner, partial branch scope and declared gates. All use270degree westward,primary10cm/s,surface>5cm/s and complete native0–200m signed-integral selection. Frozen selected-column5/10/20cm/s sensitivities are not interchangeable physical boundaries. current:south-equatorial receives no inherited measurement.",
    "Atlantic31–35W near Fernando de Noronha is partial western cSEC context, distinct from coastal NBC/NBUC and SEUC. Pacific100–140W targets a southern surface branch, distinct from equatorial/northern/subsurface currents; old142E northern-branch source depths are not transferred. Indian90–70E targets a southern zonal-mode reach and does not capture northern meanders outside gates. Source thermal/salinity fronts and instrument limits are not velocity boundaries.",
    "Exploratory windows and maxima do not independently validate named-current axes or branch membership; mesoscale or neighboring flow can affect same-sign layers. Source connector distances are not measured current lengths or widths. Neither last wet level nor bed nor missing support fills a lower contour.",
    "Frozen v18 source-to-reference and v12 adjacent-only interpolation preserve all original gates and gaps. Only adjacent eligible source nodes permit assumed lower-depth interpolation. Paired spans additionally require both resolved boundaries. No alternate-cutoff fill, weaker interior substitution, gap skipping, extrapolation or thermal promotion occurs. Unselected midpoint geometry remains explicitly unsampled.",
    "Immutable v14 base, twelve earlier addenda, all90 earlier supported scenarios, historical unresolved cases, every previous CSV cell and canonical ownership lists are preserved. The WSC interval report remains separately pinned. Inventoryv13 adds one pinned addendum/CSV without rewriting older source or numerical helper artifacts.",
    "Eleven cloud projection tests cover all6cases/30anchors, source values and pointers, frames/cutoffs/gates, geometry placeholders, selection/censoring gaps, adjacent-only interpolation, mutations and piece/input/count integrity, old data/CSV/ownership preservation and no physical/annual promotion. Six canonical baseline tests passed on the exact code commit. Source collection separately passed40 tests and audited all original sections.",
    "All acquisition, retries, geometry, selection, contour/interpolation calculations, inventory reconstruction and tests ran sequentially in cloud on one idle CPU. Local work only prepared code, reviewed primary text/metadata, checked hashes and retained exact artifacts. No local numerical field processing/tests or runtime/UI/browser work occurred; caps are unchanged.",
    "Two instantaneous2022 snapshots establish neither annual bounds nor seasonal envelopes, independent observations, confidence intervals, whole-current physical thickness, matched width/depth area, physical volume, state join or global total. Remaining coverage, observational/seasonal validation and query/runtime integration remain unfinished."
  ],
